{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass when Laban heard, etc.</b> The saying of <b>וַיְהִי</b> is in the language of distress. It alludes that he directed his intention toward evil, as they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 70:13), that he went out to rob him and searched his hidden things, and also embraced him in order to know what he had with him, and also kissed him — if in his mouth were [hidden] jewels. And the saying of <b>he heard Jacob his sister's son</b> means: Rachel did not tell what Jacob said to her, namely that he was her father's brother, but rather that he was the son of Rebecca — a righteous man son of a righteous woman. And with this he devised plans to deceive him. And also the saying of <b>he brought him to his house</b> — the reason is perhaps that his wealth would come after him, so he brought him to his house until his possessions arrive." "<b>And he told Laban all, etc.</b> The reason for his coming, and the purpose of his coming, and what befell him with Eliphaz, for he took everything from him when he pursued after him:" "<b>Further,</b> it may be explained along the lines of what they said, of blessed memory (Megillah 13b), that Rachel informed Jacob that her father was a deceiver. Therefore he was cunning to tell him all the things that had befallen him, so that through this he would refrain from doing evil when he would know how cunning he had been, to the point that he obtained the birthright and the blessing — he would know that he would outwit the cunning for whatever he might need. He also informed him of what passed at the matter of the stone, and this would tell that he was a mighty man of valor. Also the matter of watering the flocks, and this would tell of his love for him and his upright conduct with him."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:35.865359704Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}